<p>Marcelo Nicchio's time at <strong>PSINet</strong>, from June 2000 to May 2001, coincided with one of the most turbulent periods in the history of the commercial internet. But his relationship with the company's Brazilian operation had begun years earlier, back in the BBS era.</p>
<p>What began as the experience of an early user of digital communication services in Brazil would end inside a multinational whose aggressive expansion made it one of the emblematic casualties of the dot-com bubble.</p>
